# 12 October 2026: task M1, transcription of a reference into a procedural score (score.json), the measurement
# benchmark of the music 1:1 rule (Rules.md, rule-music-1to1-benchmark-20261012). Deterministic signal processing
# only: band spectral flux and peak picking (drums), pyin (monophonic bass and vocals), harmonic-constrained NMF on a
# CQT of the harmonic part of the "other" stem (polyphony, chords, sustain), novelty sections, RMS automation.
# Demucs stems are an accepted analysis input. No generative model, and the score holds numbers only: no sample of
# the reference ever leaves this module. Every threshold lives in datasets/transcribe-params.json (HDA interface).
# Score layout (version "zrmd.score/1"):
#   tempo {bpm, period, t0, firstKick, beats[{i,t,tRefined,bar,beatInBar}], bars[{index,start,end,bpm}]}
#   sections[{index,start,end,startBar,endBar,levels}]
#   drums[{t,class,velocity,levelDb,step,bar,beatInBar,stepInBar,offsetMs}]
#   voices{bass:{notes[{t,dur,midi,cents,velocity,levelDb,glide?}]}, otherLow/otherMid/otherHigh:{notes}, vocals}
#   chords[{t,end,label,root,quality,pitches,score}]
#   automation{hop, stems{drums,bass,other,vocals: [dB]}}
# render_score() plays a score with sine and noise voices (verification only, not a sound design), and evaluate()
# measures onset F-measure and chroma similarity against each stem.
# FR : transcription deterministe d'une reference en partition procedurale (score.json), banc de mesure du 1:1.
